# Overlay for the QEMU end-to-end test (tools/e2e/run_e2e.py). The emulator has no
# W5500, I2C expander, GPIO inputs or RMT, and it does not model: QIO flash reads by the
# app (data shifted by 2 bytes) and the RS485 half-duplex UART mode (uart_wait_tx_done
# asserts) and has no Wi-Fi radio. The octal PSRAM is in sdkconfig.qemu-psram (E2E_PSRAM=1,
# issue #85); this build runs without it.
# Never flash this build.
CONFIG_GW_ETH_OPENETH=y
CONFIG_GW_IO_SIMULATED=y
CONFIG_GW_RS485_HW_HALF_DUPLEX=n
CONFIG_SPIRAM=n
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_DIO=y
CONFIG_GW_WIFI=n
# CFG-7: the production NVS encryption, on the emulated HMAC peripheral and eFuse file of each
# run (nothing real is burned), so the E2E exercises it
CONFIG_NVS_ENCRYPTION=y
CONFIG_NVS_SEC_KEY_PROTECT_USING_HMAC=y
CONFIG_NVS_SEC_HMAC_EFUSE_KEY_ID=5
# QEMU writes the flash image asynchronously: a reset right after the panic handler saved the
# core dump can drop its last write (the checksum) from the image. One second lets it land.
CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_PANIC_REBOOT_DELAY_SECONDS=1
# Issue #59: the E2E slow link (700 B/s through a relay) must exceed the publish budget with
# payloads of at most 6 KB once slirp's buffers are full; 2 s does, the default 8 s would not
CONFIG_GW_MQTT_PUBLISH_BUDGET_MS=2000
# SPB-14: QEMU has no SDMMC: the store & forward spill goes to a LittleFS directory instead
CONFIG_GW_SF_SPILL_LITTLEFS=y
# FW-1: the E2E waits for a new image's trial to time out (rollback without a Sparkplug session)
CONFIG_GW_FW_CONFIRM_TIMEOUT_S=30
# FW-1: QEMU does not model the S3 cache freeze of a flash mapping; code fetched by the other
# core while an OTA image is verified makes it abort ("Bad ram pointer"): park that core
CONFIG_GW_FW_PARK_OTHER_CORE=y
# FW-2: OTA images must carry a valid RSA-3072 signature (Secure Boot V2 format) as in
# production, but without hardware Secure Boot: esp_ota_end() runs the same verification with
# the key taken from the running app instead of eFuse. Nothing is burned. The test key is
# generated by run_e2e.sh in build-qemu/ (never committed).
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_NO_SECURE_BOOT=y
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_RSA_SCHEME=y
CONFIG_SECURE_SIGNED_ON_UPDATE_NO_SECURE_BOOT=y
CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT_BUILD_SIGNED_BINARIES=y
CONFIG_SECURE_BOOT_SIGNING_KEY="build-qemu/e2e_signing_key.pem"
# FW-1: no USB-Serial-JTAG secondary console (QEMU has no USB host anyway). Its connection
# monitor runs in every tick interrupt and reads the USB peripheral; on the core parked during
# an image verification that read faulted under QEMU's cache freeze (LoadStorePIFAddrError)
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_SECONDARY_NONE=y
# Issue #113: the emulated open_eth MAC has 4 RX DMA buffers by default (1 600 B each); under
# the E2E's full-speed uploads slirp's bursts overflow them ("RX frame dropped (0x14)"), and a
# lost SYN is retried by slirp only after its backoff, past the harness client's 15 s (#110).
# 6: in 60 --web-stress rounds 0 frames dropped (58 with 4) for 3.2 KB more internal RAM; the
# #80 case keeps its largest block at the validation at 24 576 B (27 648 B with 4; threshold
# 17 KB). 10 (sdkconfig.qemu-psram) costs too much of that margin here. QEMU only: the board's
# W5500 has its own 16 KB of RX buffer.
CONFIG_ETH_OPENETH_DMA_RX_BUFFER_NUM=6
